    "summary": "Woman&#039;s lip-ornament, labret made of alder wood. Carved from a horizontal, oval section of wood to form a narrow plug, relatively tall, for a relatively young woman, with deep depressions top and bottom to lighten the weight, and flanges at the top, and particularly at the ends to hold the plug in place. A section of the plug (ca. 2cm by 5mm) broke away at the top, after registration, and is now missing.",
